<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Spartacus.jpg" alt="A portrait of a mastiff" width="550" height="563" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Spartacus. 14x14, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">It has been a busy last couple of days: painted this portrait, started another, finished another, made changes to two others, painted a color study, stretched and primed two canvases, then toned 6 panels.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">I painted this sketch portrait from the customer's own photos: the larger square format made a nice fit for Spartacus's big boxy head. Leaving the bottom of the canvas unfinished helped to balance out the mass of his noggin in the upper half of the painting.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">I used a palette of ultramarine, alizarin permanent, cad orange and cad yellow medium, plus a small amount of bright red in the collar and a small amount of burnt sienna mixed with ultramarine for the darkest bits.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">After consultation with the customer I made a few small changes to the eye area.</p>